{# ── Hero stage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The motion is not a boxed illustration beside a text column: it is the
   hero's full field, and the copy sits on it.

   THE FILM IS OURS. It is authored in tools/hero-film from this site's own
   tokens, typefaces and layout language and rendered at build time, so the
   subject is a business presence being formed — intent, identity, digital
   surfaces, readiness — and not a licensed architectural scene that read as a
   property campaign.

   FOUR VARIANTS, ONE DOWNLOAD. The film carries real words, so it cannot be
   mirrored with a CSS transform the way an abstract frame could: each
   direction is composed, not flipped. The locale is known at build time, so
   only that locale's pair is ever referenced, and orientation picks one of the
   two within it. Portrait phones get the 4:5 cut, whose action sits in the
   band left exposed below the copy; everything else gets the 16:9 cut.

   Poster-first by construction: the <source> elements carry data-src, not src,
   so a <video autoplay> with no resolvable source downloads NOTHING until JS
   decides motion is both permitted (not reduced-motion, not Save-Data) and
   needed (near the viewport, tab visible). Reduced motion, Save-Data and no-JS
   therefore cost zero video bytes rather than "load, then stop".

   The poster IS the film's last frame, rendered from the same scene at the
   same timestamp, so the resting state and the finished state can never drift
   apart. The film does NOT loop: it plays once and comes to rest on that
   frame, and the control becomes a replay.

   The poster <img> carries intrinsic width/height inside a sized stage, so
   there is no black frame, no blank frame and no layout shift. The video sits
   on top at opacity 0 and is revealed only once it is genuinely playing, and
   it is inset by 1px so the poster stays strictly the larger element and
   therefore always wins LCP. Do not remove that inset without re-measuring. #}
{% set film = "he" if loc.dir == "rtl" else "en" %}
<div class="hero-stage" data-hero-motion aria-hidden="true">
  <picture class="hero-stage-poster">
    <source media="(max-width:860px) and (orientation:portrait)"
            srcset="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-poster-{{ film }}-mobile.webp" type="image/webp">
    <img src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-poster-{{ film }}-desktop.webp" alt=""
         width="1280" height="720" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high">
  </picture>

  <video class="hero-stage-video" autoplay muted playsinline preload="none"
         disablepictureinpicture disableremoteplayback tabindex="-1">
    <source media="(max-width:860px) and (orientation:portrait)"
            data-src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-motion-{{ film }}-mobile.webm" type="video/webm">
    <source data-src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-motion-{{ film }}-desktop.webm" type="video/webm">
    <source media="(max-width:860px) and (orientation:portrait)"
            data-src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-motion-{{ film }}-mobile.mp4" type="video/mp4">
    <source data-src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-motion-{{ film }}-desktop.mp4" type="video/mp4">
  </video>

  {# Two scrims: one along the copy edge for contrast, one at the foot so the
     stage resolves into the page instead of ending on a hard line. #}
  <span class="hero-scrim-edge"></span>
  <span class="hero-scrim-foot"></span>
</div>
